<title>CANADA: Canada's XCan Grain forecasts 97/98 canola supply.</title>
<headline>Canada's XCan Grain forecasts 97/98 canola supply.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>XCan Grain Ltd on Monday forecast canola ending stocks in crop year 1997/98 (Aug/July) would reach 1.398 million tonnes compared to an estimated 368,000 tonnes expected by July 31, 1997, in a supply and demand table issued at the Canadian Wheat Board's annual conference here.</p>
<p>	  CANADIAN CANOLA SUPPLY &amp; DEMAND (in '000 tonnes)</p>
<p>    SUPPLY   1995/96   1996/97   1997/98</p>
<p>    Stocks     589	 925	 368</p>
<p>    Output   6,436     5,037     7,000</p>
<p>    Imports     97	  96	  40</p>
<p>    Total    7,123     6,058     7,408</p>
<p>DISPOSITION</p>
<p>    Exports  2,804     2,390     2,400</p>
<p>    Seed	  27	  40	  40</p>
<p>    Dom.Crush2,753     2,628     2,700</p>
<p>    Waste	639	 632	 878</p>
<p>    Total    6,222     5,690     6,018</p>
<p>    Carry out  901	 368     1,398</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras (204) 947 3548))</p>
</text>
